---
layout: default
# WEB-34. The one page on cascadras.com, for the Cascadras demand test,
# rebuilt to Mandy's (Art & Design Director) approved mockup. Copy is the
# WEB-34 spec's, word for word (Lee's calls, 2026-11-21): no founders'
# price, "Planned price" next to every price, no date anywhere.
---
<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">
        <svg width="26" height="20" viewBox="0 0 26 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 19 L9 6 L13 12 L17 3 L25 19 Z" fill="#8FD3C5"/><path d="M15.2 6.6 L17 3 L18.8 6.6 L17.6 6 L17 7 L16.4 6 Z" fill="#fff"/></svg>
        Cascadras
      </a>
      <a class="nav-cta" href="#reserve" data-fathom-click="cascadras-reserve-click">Reserve a founding seat →</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="pill"><span class="dot"></span>Under development · Founding seats open</div>
        <h1>Your team made that decision. Can anyone find out why?</h1>
        <p class="lede">We're building Cascadras: one place for your team's architecture decisions. Write them, review them, approve them, and find them again, across every repo. Your risk matrix and service tiers live right beside them.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn" href="#reserve" data-fathom-click="cascadras-reserve-click">Reserve a founding seat</a>
          <div class="price-block">
            <div class="price-line">$19 per architect a month <span>· everyone else reads free</span></div>
            <span class="planned">Planned price. We'll never charge you without your OK.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="founding-note">Founding seats are the first to try it, and their feedback shapes what we build. No card, and nothing starts without your OK.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="sketch" role="img" aria-label="An early sketch of a Cascadras decision record">
        <div class="sketch-label">EARLY SKETCH · UNDER DEVELOPMENT</div>
        <div class="card" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="top"><span class="id">ADR-014 · payments-api</span><span class="tag ok">Accepted</span></div>
          <h4>Move session state to Redis</h4>
          <div class="meta"><span class="tag">Tier 1</span><span class="tag">Owner: Platform team</span><span class="tag">Reviewed by 3</span></div>
          <div class="why">Sticky sessions block scaling past four nodes. Redis lets any node serve any request.</div>
          <div class="links">
            <div class="row"><span>Reduces <b>R-07</b> Session loss on deploy</span><span class="tag hi">High → Low</span></div>
            <div class="row"><span>Creates <b>R-12</b> Redis is a new single point</span><span class="tag">Medium</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="foot"><span class="mono">docs/adr/0014-redis-sessions.md</span><span>Supersedes ADR-006</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card2" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="row"><span class="mono muted">Risk matrix</span><span class="tag hi">3 High</span></div>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top:6px"><span>Each risk linked to its decisions</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap problem-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">The problem</div>
      <h2>Decisions get made in meetings, Slack threads and pull requests. Then they get lost.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="quote">Six months later, someone asks why the system works this way. Nobody knows.</p>
      <p>The person who decided has moved on, and the reasons went with them.</p>
      <p>Some teams keep decision records. Most keep them as markdown files spread across a dozen repos, or as wiki pages nobody can find. Free tools help you write a record. Few help your team review it, approve it, and find it again.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">What you'll get</div>
    <h2>Records first. Everything else links to them.</h2>
    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="feat">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 3h9l3 3v15H6z"/><path d="M9 9h6M9 13h6M9 17h4"/></svg>
        <h3>Decision records <span class="lees">Lee's templates</span></h3>
        <p>Write, review, approve and search. Every repo, one place. Start from Lee Atchison's templates, or bring your own.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M3 15h18M9 3v18M15 3v18"/></svg>
        <h3>Risk matrices, linked <span class="lees">From Lee's book</span></h3>
        <p>Each risk links to the decisions that create it or reduce it, and to the service it lives in. No more stale spreadsheet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18h16M6 14h12M8 10h8M10 6h4"/></svg>
        <h3>Service tiers</h3>
        <p>Tag each service Tier 1 to Tier 4, or name your own. The tier shows on every decision, every risk, and the map.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6" cy="6" r="2.5"/><circle cx="18" cy="6" r="2.5"/><circle cx="12" cy="18" r="2.5"/><path d="M8 7l3 9M16 7l-3 9M8.5 6h7"/></svg>
        <h3>Who owns what</h3>
        <p>Which team owns which service, who's on call, and where the runbook is. It comes free with the records.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6" cy="5" r="2"/><circle cx="6" cy="19" r="2"/><circle cx="18" cy="12" r="2"/><path d="M6 7v10M6 12h10"/></svg>
        <h3>Your records stay yours</h3>
        <p>Git is the backend. Clone, pull, push, export. Already keep Nygard or MADR records? Import them on day one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 9l-4 3 4 3M16 9l4 3-4 3M13 6l-2 12"/></svg>
        <h3>Your AI tools can read them</h3>
        <p>A built-in MCP server lets Claude Code, Cursor and the rest read your decisions while they work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Why reserve now</div>
    <h2>Cascadras is under development. Help us get it right.</h2>
    <div class="founding">
      <div class="fitem">
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <h3>Be among the first to try it</h3>
        <p>Founding seats get early versions before anyone else.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fitem">
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <h3>Shape where it goes</h3>
        <p>Tell us how your team works. Founding members' feedback shapes what gets built first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fitem">
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <h3>No commitment</h3>
        <p>No card, no payment, and nothing happens automatically. When it's ready, you decide whether to sign up.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="who"><span><strong>Made for engineering teams of about 10 to 50 engineers.</strong> Big enough to lose track of why things were built the way they were. Too small for a heavyweight developer portal.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap price-wrap">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">The price</div>
      <h2>Pay for the people who write the records.</h2>
      <p>Usually one to three architects per team. Everyone else reads and comments for free.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card">
      <div class="big">$19 <small>per architect a month</small></div>
      <span class="planned">Planned price. We'll never charge you without your OK.</span>
      <ul>
        <li>Readers and commenters free</li>
        <li>Git-backed, export any time</li>
        <li>Founding seats try it first</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn dark" href="#reserve" data-fathom-click="cascadras-reserve-click">Reserve a founding seat</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section band">
  <div class="wrap lee-wrap">
    <div class="lee">
      <img class="photo" src="/images/lee-atchison.png" alt="Lee Atchison" width="120" height="120" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">From Lee Atchison</div>
        <p>I've spent years writing and teaching about architecture decisions and risk. I'm building Cascadras to put that thinking into a tool your team can use every day. Its risk matrix is the one from <i>Architecting for Scale</i>.</p>
        <p class="sig">Lee Atchison · author of <i>Architecting for Scale</i> and <i>The Software Conductor</i>, and the Software Architecture Insights newsletter</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="reserve">
  <div class="wrap">
    <%= render "reserve_form", form_id: site.metadata.kit_form_id %>
  </div>
</section>
